{
  "id": "runner_03_first_run",
  "side": "Runner",
  "title": "Your first run",
  "intro": "A run is how you attack a server. It has six phases: initiation, approach ice, encounter ice, movement, success, and run ends. With no ice in the way you go straight from initiation to success and access the server's cards.\n\nArchives is the Corp's discard pile, and the Corp discarded a card last turn. This lesson: run Archives and walk through the phases — watch the strip in the coaching panel.",
  "outro": "A successful run on Archives lets you access every card in it. Nothing there scores, but Archives is a real target: agendas the Corp was forced to discard are stolen from there. Next: running through ice.",
  "corp_deck": "the_syndicate_starter",
  "runner_deck": "the_catalyst_starter",
